    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# RSS Read Node\n1. Manual Trigger \n2. RSS Read Node\n-- Contains an RSS link with specified search terms obtained from PubMed.\n-- Pulls 15 most recent pharmacological research on Ketamine (as JSON).\n3. Loop-Over-Items + Post + Wait loop\n--  Can't post 15 items to Discord because of rate limits.\n--  15 posts separated into batches of 1, posted 1 at a time with 0.5s in between posts.\n3. Discord POST\n-- REST API (POST) node \n-- Posts to Discord server via a webhook\n-- JSON is used in body of REST request\n4. Final Output: \n-- 15 posts in a Discord server",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 2048,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -784,
        -864
      ],
      "id": "0aa355fd-d79b-417f-a3d7-e90344a987f7",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# RSS Feed Node\n1. RSS Feed Trigger\n-- Runs every minute\n-- Keeps track of previously posted items and only posts new items that hit the feed\n-- RSS link is still set to 15 so maximum output here is 15\n2. Loop-Over-Items + Post + Wait loop\n-- Same deal as above, to work around rate limits.\n3. Final Output\n-- 0-15 posts contingent on new articles entering PubMed matching the RSS links\nsearch terms\n\n# ISSUES\n1. RSS feed trigger fails to only post new items\n2. Scheduled trigger workaround also fails to post new items\n\nMy idea ended up being to create a postgres table to persist data and manually filter for diffs\n",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 1648,
        "color": 7
      },
